      "content": "<h3>containsValue(Object) and contains(Object)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Signature:</strong> <code>boolean containsValue(Object value);  boolean contains(Object value)</code></li>\n<li><strong>Returns:</strong> boolean</li>\n<li><strong>Time:</strong> O(n)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>For freshers:</strong> Both ask \"does any pair have this value?\". <code>contains</code> is the legacy name and does <strong>exactly the same</strong> as <code>containsValue</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>For experienced developers:</strong> It scans every bucket, so it is slow on big tables. Beware: <code>contains</code> checks <em>values</em>, not keys, which surprises people used to <code>Collection.contains</code>.</p>",
